                                    .page-text
                                        h5 id="disclaimer"
                                    h6 style="display: none" id="disclaimer-hidden"
                                        |
                                            Everything you see or hear in this talk is purely fictional and not connected to any real company I’ve ever come across.
                                            Also, the examples are for demonstration only ✨ (and yes… there may be much better design approaches 🙃).
                                    / .page-footer 1
                            
                            .page-slide
                                .page-content
                            
                            .page-slide
                                .page-content
                                    h2.page-header Once upon a ⌚...
                                    .page-text
                                        h5
                                            |
                                                There was a little 🏢, and this 🏢 had an intelligent CTO who just hated templates <😈>.<br><br>

                                                There was always the assumption that 😈s are difficult to maintain and that it's much harder
                                                to 🕵🏼‍♀️ someone who 💡 how to 💻 with them.<br><br>

                                                At the <- it all seemed so easy, as the idea was simply 💡💡💡 -
                                                to create a list of 🍓 to collect in the 🌲🌲 before going out and forgetting what was needed.<br><br>
                                    / .page-footer 3
                            
                            .page-slide
                                .page-content
                                    .page-text
                                        h5 So their technology looked like that:<br><br>
                                        .r-stack
                                            pre.larger-font
                                                code.hljs.cpp data-trim="" data-line-numbers=""
                                                    script type="text/template"
                                                        |
                                                            class grocery {
                                                                std::string name;
                                                            };

                                                            class basket {
                                                                grocery groceries[5];
                                                            };
                                        h5
                                            |
                                                <br><br>After completing the product, there was no need for a team to 🛠️ it, and the team was able to std::move std::forward to other technology challenges.
                                    / .page-footer 4
                                    / TODO: Add a picture of a small basket with groceries

                            .page-slide
                                .page-content
                                    h2.page-header Modern 🧺
                                    .page-text
                                        h4
                                            |
                                                ⌚ 🚶🏽‍♀️ by and an invention of a new modern 🧺 aimed to destroy the company 🥇s.<br>
                                                A modern 🧺 which can contain up to <b>10</b> 🍇 at the same time!<br><br>

                            .page-slide
                                .page-content
                                    .page-text
                                        h4 
                                            |
                                                But the company CTO was not about to 🏳️, she moved back her team to this product and together created a newer
                                                list named <b>modern_basket</b>:<br><br>
                                        pre.larger-font 
                                            code.hljs.cpp data-trim="" data-line-numbers=""
                                                script type="text/template"
                                                    |
                                                        class modern_basket {
                                                            grocery groceries[10];
                                                        };
                                        / TODO: Add a picture of a large basket with groceries

                                    / .page-footer 5

                            .page-slide 
                                .page-content 
                                    h2.page-header Extremely Truly Absolutely Modern 🧺
                                    .page-text 
                                        h5 
                                            |
                                                The new 💡 👆🏽 the company's stock price 📈, and everything
                                                seemed so peaceful for the company, until a newer 💡 got the attention of the 🌎.<br><br>
                                                A 🛒!<br><br>
                                                This 🛒 was able to contian up to <b>50</b> (🤯) 🍄‍🟫s at the same time.
                                    / .page-footer 6

                            .page-slide 
                                .page-content 
                                    .page-text 
                                        h5 
                                            |
                                                The CTO was 😫.<br><br>
                                                She and the team 🔎 it frustrating to create each time a new moderner modern container.<br>
                                                She knew they needed something 🧠, more dynamic and flexible.<br>
                                                And in times of despair, she decided to do the inevitable upgrade to their architecture:

                                        pre.fragment.current-visible data-id="code-animation-1" data-fragment-index="0"
                                        pre.larger-font.fragment data-id="code-animation-1" data-fragment-index="1"
                                            code.hljs.cpp data-trim="" data-line-numbers=""
                                                script type="text/template"
                                                    |
                                                        template <size_t Capacity>
                                                        class groceries_container {
                                                            grocery groceries[Capacity];
                                                        };
                                    / .page-footer 7

                            .page-slide 
                                .page-content 
                                    .page-text 
                                        h5 id="book-ending"
                                    h6 style="display: none" id="book-ending-hidden"
                                        |
                                            And from that moment on, things were never as before.

                                            The company started to use more <😇> code.
                                            They learned constexpr, consteval, fold-expressions, reflection (well, soon...).
                                            They built compile time tools and features.

                                            Their company grew.
                                            And the CTO was finally happy —
                                            because she never had to write the std::next extremely_truly_moderner_basket.
                                    / .page-footer 9

